Start the program
Import the re module
Define a string with a phone number
Use re.search() to find a 10-digit number
If found, display the number
Define another string with marks
Use re.findall() to extract all numbers
Display the list of numbers
Define a string starting with "Hello"
Use re.match() to check the beginning of the string
If matched, display the message
Define a string with the word "apples"
Use re.sub() to replace "apples" with "oranges"
Display the modified string
Stop the program

code 

import re
text = "My number is 9876543210"
result = re.search(r"\d{10}", text)
if result:
    print("Number found:", result.group())
text2 = "Marks are 85, 90 and 78"
numbers = re.findall(r"\d+", text2)
print("All numbers:", numbers)
text3 = "Hello Python"
if re.match(r"Hello", text3):
    print("Starts with Hello")
text4 = "I like apples"
new_text = re.sub(r"apples", "oranges", text4)
print("After replacement:", new_text)

Output

